    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 331,
        "text": "Good evening. Tonight we ask a simple but difficult question: when does the public's right to know beat a person's right to privacy? Our panel has three guests. Dr. Lin, a media lawyer. Mr. Carter, a former newspaper editor. And Ms. Okafor, a data-protection adviser. Dr. Lin, you wrote a report last year. What did you find?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "3f6e9a7efb70dd1802d8a420d8f41e2cb719b23571d7e393a1c271bae3f6b7df",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "dr lin",
        "speaker": "Dr. Lin",
        "sourceStart": 342,
        "sourceEnd": 629,
        "text": "We looked at forty court cases. In most of them, the judge said the public interest was strong because the story showed a real risk to safety. But in twelve cases, the judge said the privacy claim was stronger. The reason was simple: the information was only embarrassing, not dangerous.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "0f4c7a857845564b232dfcb9f7cd0a19263bc9ef4a746e43383549d1d1d42232",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 637,
        "sourceEnd": 740,
        "text": "Mr. Carter, you edited a paper for twenty years. Did you ever publish a story that you later regretted?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "70eb0f7c10311ee3950a7d910dccf20ec4264f6b868e5bdba9e0554b0dcdbf34",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr carter",
        "speaker": "Mr. Carter",
        "sourceStart": 754,
        "sourceEnd": 982,
        "text": "Yes, once. We ran a story about a teacher who had a second job. The story was true, but it was not important. The teacher lost her job, and I still feel bad about it. That was a mistake. We should have asked: who does this help?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "c128c2443ff034daeefb844017fb02024f2d62e35aea8f92f43187f1323e7b8f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ms okafor",
        "speaker": "Ms. Okafor",
        "sourceStart": 996,
        "sourceEnd": 1348,
        "text": "I agree with that question. But I want to add a warning. A story that seems small can become big online. Last month, a hospital shared a patient's name by accident. The name was in a file that a journalist received. The journalist did not publish it, and that was the right choice. The public did not need the name. The public needed the safety report.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "6eb5a898989c5992da45d3b6208b42e06c10d6c22cf37aa675732845eeff7417",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1356,
        "sourceEnd": 1387,
        "text": "Dr. Lin, is there a clear rule?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "ce08da126225e3e8ea781aa64d615cd0b4cd18d0e9da0904b215f4fd9f5cbbdc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "dr lin",
        "speaker": "Dr. Lin",
        "sourceStart": 1398,
        "sourceEnd": 1676,
        "text": "There is no single rule. But courts often ask three things. First, is the person powerful or public? Second, is the fact private or already known? Third, will publishing stop harm or cause harm? If the answer to the last question is 'cause harm', the privacy claim usually wins.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "5fec5a2b632d4fcb1091b6d51b191c3a8132a42653189fc966e44263c64c4404",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr carter",
        "speaker": "Mr. Carter",
        "sourceStart": 1690,
        "sourceEnd": 1901,
        "text": "I would add a fourth question: can we tell the story without the private detail? Often we can. When I was an editor, we sometimes changed a name or a street. The story still worked. Readers understood the point.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "1404668542115fff05ad59237ebc05772be3365e87ad9d9a966f29b8821d7a05",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ms okafor",
        "speaker": "Ms. Okafor",
        "sourceStart": 1915,
        "sourceEnd": 2193,
        "text": "That is a good practice. But I want to be fair to journalists. Some stories are important because of a name. If a mayor uses public money for a private trip, the name matters. The public interest is strong there. The difference is that the mayor is responsible for public money.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "86a6c86f55bf82ea203f20e43bd1e9daab6de53d027bb1c52ced351925899057",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 2201,
        "sourceEnd": 2231,
        "text": "So the line is responsibility?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "ccde0b9eec5b25d045196c54c222d82f032d4d97037eaa7d53c60fc1fe235e0a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ms okafor",
        "speaker": "Ms. Okafor",
        "sourceStart": 2245,
        "sourceEnd": 2415,
        "text": "Partly. Responsibility, power, and harm. If a person has power and the fact shows harm, publish. If the person has no power and the fact only embarrasses, do not publish.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "3d8de3df31d27c11e6d9a03e6a4e01c46cf2a6bf5c73a3c5862acbf33f0bb1ac",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "dr lin",
        "speaker": "Dr. Lin",
        "sourceStart": 2426,
        "sourceEnd": 2578,
        "text": "I would say 'usually do not publish'. There can be exceptions. But the burden should be on the publisher to explain why the private detail is necessary.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "d0ec0fc274859e084ae842fe5d6e8283210de4922e4cb5aad89a43ab230c7e21",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr carter",
        "speaker": "Mr. Carter",
        "sourceStart": 2592,
        "sourceEnd": 2737,
        "text": "And that explanation should be public. When we published the teacher story, we did not explain why. We just said it was true. True is not enough.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a5cfbef53aae2b3f903c616cbd5d8661459a456c20387ccb8e3b81756f8bbd9c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 2745,
        "sourceEnd": 2807,
        "text": "One last question. What should a young journalist do tomorrow?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5dc625a2c5f893e369b2fb146c4d0a6b74715329ece604672e0724d77eb71fab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ms okafor",
        "speaker": "Ms. Okafor",
        "sourceStart": 2821,
        "sourceEnd": 2987,
        "text": "Ask three questions before you publish. Who is hurt? Who is helped? Is the private detail necessary? Write the answers down. If you cannot write them, do not publish.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "7226907bb3c3d50bf7668472efb527d0e0372e41a4e66821bc484d6d63f21ace",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mr carter",
        "speaker": "Mr. Carter",
        "sourceStart": 3001,
        "sourceEnd": 3072,
        "text": "And talk to your editor early. Do not wait until the story is finished.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "e6c40dd3a9ddd4d8f3cc1d765ca8793acd2db30d65699fd6d8ee65529513fc6b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "dr lin",
        "speaker": "Dr. Lin",
        "sourceStart": 3083,
        "sourceEnd": 3152,
        "text": "And keep a record. A record protects you and the person in the story.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "c8f98a86e72de416dfdd29d1ce5e8cf30bb8428efe958c7adaf23b0fc25745dc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 3160,
        "sourceEnd": 3206,
        "text": "Thank you all. That is a useful place to stop.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "7b88c30030b1b284345b33ba2bffcfc29f6db6162500477b0c4525ca5c8bdda6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
